;; The files of repr/python's round trip (bin/repr-python roundtrip, levels 1-3: roundtrip-known.edn, CPython's levels 2-3,
;; live and the oracle tier's; roundtrip-own-known.edn, levels 2-3 by pyi's own ast and compile, records mode; roundtrip --text,
;; levels 4-5: full-known.edn; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: PY2", "As built: PY3") that do not pass every
;; level, by corpus, each with its class (:classes, each with what it is and the decision it rests on). Written by
;; --record, the classes kept; the writer classes a file only by rule (:rejected, :code-lines, :own-code-lines, :charset) and never
;; writes a guess: a file of no class makes the run exit 3. Read with the Clojure reader.
{:classes
 {:own-code-lines
  {:decided "by design, as :code-lines (queue 175's DECISION (a)) for pyi's compiler: queue 431's DECISION 2 (a), pending the user's", :what "levels 1 and 2 by pyi pass (the forms and pyi's ast without attributes are equal) but pyi's code objects of the print differ from the original's after own-norm-code: pyi's compiler ports CPython's line passes (arbace.python.compile's flow!), whose output depends on the lines a statement spans beyond the :nop instructions the normalization drops"}
  :rejected
  {:decided "the survey's §5.3 (PYS3 (a)): the read level's reference is CPython's acceptance and message", :what "CPython's ast.parse rejects the file (a deliberately bad file of Lib/test: an unknown or wrong encoding, a character no identifier takes): the read gives (python/error CLASS MSG ...), judged on CPython's class and message (survey §5.3); nothing to print"}}
